            <ArticleTitle>Morphologic and functional assessment of coronary aneurysm after Kawasaki disease by repeated dipyridamole-loading coronary angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>387-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The long-term outcome of coronary aneurysm after Kawasaki disease was investigated using dipyridamole-loading angiography in 33 children with coronary aneurysms after Kawasaki disease. Morphologic regression may not accompany functional improvement in the dilated coronary arteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
